@docs_styles navbar, section, theme_head, sidebar, sync_navigation, sidebar_id

[$in title:["Documentation"]]
[$in description:["Moth language, project and compiler documentation."]]
[$in head:[theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
listed = sync_navigation(sidebar_id)!
[section, $md:
    # Documentation

    Start with @./language-overview (Language basics) to see how field lists, constructors, brackets and blocks fit together. The @./cheatsheet (cheatsheet) collects the same forms for reference.

    These pages describe the syntax being introduced on this branch. Compiler and MON support for the new spellings is still pending.

    The @./progress (compiler progress matrix) tracks current language, compiler and backend coverage.
    The @./progress/packages-and-builders (packages and builders progress matrix) tracks first-party
    packages and project-builder capabilities.

    ## Start here

    1. @./getting-started (Getting Started)
    2. @./language-overview (Language basics)
    3. @./bindings (Values and bindings)
    4. @./numbers (Numbers)
    5. @./casts (Casts)
    6. @./functions (Functions)
    7. @./branching (Branching)
    8. @./loops (Loops)
    9. @./structs (Structs and methods)
    10. @./choices (Choices)
    11. @./errors (Errors, options and assertions)
    12. @./collections (Collections and maps)
    13. @./templates (Templates)
    14. @./template-directives (Template directives)
    15. @./constants (Constants and compile-time behaviour)
    16. @./aliases (Aliases)
    17. @./generics (Generics)
    18. @./traits (Traits)
    19. @./wiring (Wiring)
    20. @./memory (Memory and lifetimes)

    ## Projects and content

    - @./directives (Directives)
    - @./project-structure (Project structure)
    - @./packages (Packages and dependencies)
    - @./packages/core (Core packages)
    - @./resources (Resources and file values)
    - @./moth-templates (Moth template files)
    - @./markdown (Plain Markdown)
    - @./mon (MON format)
    - @./design-scope (Design scope)

    ## Moth Patterns

    - @./patterns/ (Moth Patterns): larger projects, reusable components and browser applications

    ## Quick reference

    - @./cheatsheet (Language cheatsheet): the whole language surface on one page

    ## Compiler internals

    The @../developer-docs (Developers) section covers the compiler and build
    system for contributors and anyone reading the internals.

    - @../developer-docs/compiler-design (Compiler design)
    - @../developer-docs/memory-management (Memory management)
    - @../developer-docs/style-guide (Development standards)

    ## Tasks and native runtime design

    - @./async (Channels and tasks)
    - @./lappet (Lappet native runtime and package infrastructure)
